From 06bfcd889b7a4b728d0724bdf97e997005b9ec90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: praveen <praveenkumar.shanmugam@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:02:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] GPUOP-1132: Implement partial power frames and per-subscriber
 queue

No push cap: every smi-power tick sends each subscriber a partial
GPUWatch frame (Spec with only Id, empty Attribute; Stats with only the
POWER attrs refreshed that tick; Status.MissedTicks) through a bounded
per-subscriber queue drained by the subscriber's own gRPC thread. No
watcher thread calls Write any more.

- aga_gpu_watch_power_frame_t / aga_gpu_watch_power_gpu_t frame POD;
  the client ctxt gains queue, write_power_cb and write_failed;
  subscribe_req gains write_power_cb.
- gpu_watch_sub_queue_t: SPSC ring of AGA_GPU_WATCH_SUB_QUEUE_DEPTH
  (256) preallocated slots (producer smi-power, consumer gRPC thread),
  full-frame mailbox (latest unsent frame per watch) and a wake
  semaphore. A full ring drops the newest frame; drops and replaced
  full frames count in the subscriber's MissedTicks.
- smi-power fans out one partial frame per subscriber after the
  record writes: no allocation, task, proto or Write per tick.
- aga_gpu_watch_subscribe runs smi_watch_sub_writer_loop: full frames
  first, then the ring in order; a failed write sets write_failed and
  the smi-watcher removes the subscriber within one 1 s tick. A
  subscribe the backend rejects (queue allocation failure) returns.
- amdsmi/gim/wsl: gpu_watch_notify_subscribers(fast_due, skip_power)
  reaps failed subscribers every tick and enqueues one shared full
  frame per watch; at sub-second periods the POWER attrs are left out
  of full frames. The amdsmi power view carries the live queues.
- svc: aga_gpu_watch_power_frame_to_proto, full frames add the drop
  count to MissedTicks, write_power_cb registered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
